WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:10.290
This is going to be my final Direct Message
of 2017.

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:14.960
Last week we put up 5 shows in 5 days for
Rubin Report YouTube week, this week we've

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:20.240
got my sit down with former National Public
Radio CEO Ken Stern, and next week we'll be

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.320
highlighting some of my favorite episodes
of the year.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:26.080
Today's Direct Message is going to be quick
and to the point.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:31.250
With incredible gratitude and a humble heart
I want to thank all of you helped make 2017

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:33.870
such a memorable year here at The Rubin Report.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:38.200
The ride to get here, from 12 years of stand
up comedy in NYC, to my pop culture radio

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:45.489
show at SiriusXM, to hosting on The Young
Turks to joining Larry King on OraTV and finally

00:00:45.489 --> 00:00:51.592
to this independent show funded by you, has
been a long windy journey....one which I wouldn't

00:00:51.592 --> 00:00:53.670
trade in for anything.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:56.770
It's only been a year and a half since we
made the move to independence, and as some

00:00:56.770 --> 00:01:00.860
of you have heard me say, the night before
we launched on Patreon, I literally thought

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:05.329
my career, as well as the careers of my team,
might be over.

00:01:05.329 --> 00:01:10.420
Fortunately within hours of launching we quickly
realized that not only was it not over, but

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:12.229
we were just at the beginning.

00:01:12.229 --> 00:01:16.450
In the 18 months since then, I bought a home
in which we built this totally professional

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:21.970
home studio, we expanded the team behind the
scenes, the show absolutely exploded with

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:29.030
almost 400,000 new subscribers and most importantly,
we've continued to have honest, civil conversation

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:34.200
that hopefully has left you feel a little
more enlightened and a lot less alone.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:37.610
This year we did an on location shoot with
Ayaan Hirsi Ali.

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:41.620
I interviewed Richard Dawkins in front of
a live studio audience in New York City, we

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:46.659
helped put important voices fighting for academic
freedom on the map like Jordan Petersen, Bret

00:01:46.659 --> 00:01:48.729
Weinstein and Lindsay Shephard.

00:01:48.729 --> 00:01:53.540
We hosted a conversation on religion and morality
with Dennis Prager and Michael Shermer.

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:59.400
We introduced you to incredible voices fighting
for liberalism like Yamine Mohammed and Lubna

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:00.400
Ahmed.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:04.750
We also introduced you to some previous guests
like Peter Boghossian, Eric Weinstein and

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:09.899
Gad Saad, all of whom are great guests, but
more importantly have become great friends

00:02:09.899 --> 00:02:10.899
as well.

00:02:10.899 --> 00:02:15.780
And of course, we also hosted the infamous
debate between Blaire White and Candace Owens,

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:20.779
which got me trending on Twitter for the first
time in my life, hashtag Save Dave.

00:02:20.779 --> 00:02:24.579
Your support also allowed me to take some
time off in August to work on my book and

00:02:24.579 --> 00:02:28.859
take 30 truly life changing days off the grid.

00:02:28.859 --> 00:02:34.059
In an age when we never get off our devices,
when we're slammed with news about terrorism

00:02:34.059 --> 00:02:38.889
right after we scroll past a cat video and
a picture of your high school friends new

00:02:38.889 --> 00:02:44.510
baby, you guys gave me the greatest gift I
could ask for...a little time to reset and

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:45.510
rejuvenate.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:50.239
And in exchange for you giving me some of
that precious time, we made sure to have all

00:02:50.239 --> 00:02:54.760
new shows for you throughout August ready
to roll while we were gone.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.999
I've got a long list of people to thank for
making everything happen here, but I have

00:02:57.999 --> 00:03:03.319
to give personal shout outs to David, Amiria,
Alexis, Talia and Emma.

00:03:03.319 --> 00:03:06.760
There's an incredible amount of work that
goes into producing these shows and the only

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:11.799
reason it looks easy is because of the team
that I have helping me make it look just that

00:03:11.799 --> 00:03:12.799
way.

00:03:12.799 --> 00:03:16.519
I also want to give a special shout-out to
those of you who provide us with monthly support

00:03:16.519 --> 00:03:22.450
on Patreon and PayPay, or who have done one
time donations via Bitcoin.

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:26.669
Your support not only keeps us independent,
but has given me the luxury of saying no to

00:03:26.669 --> 00:03:29.069
several big money offers this year.

00:03:29.069 --> 00:03:33.699
As long as that support remains, I see no
reason to change that, and I promise I will

00:03:33.699 --> 00:03:37.439
do my best to make sure to continue to earn
that very support.

00:03:37.439 --> 00:03:41.650
And of course, thanks to all of you who watch,
share and like these videos.

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:46.459
We've never put a dollar into YouTube ads,
but the show continues to grow because you

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:47.819
help it do so.

00:03:47.819 --> 00:03:51.489
The emails that I get from you saying how
you're putting the ideas we discuss here into

00:03:51.489 --> 00:03:55.879
action, or changing what you believe because
of something you've heard, or just are talking

00:03:55.879 --> 00:04:01.049
to people in a new way because of the tone
we've set here is incredibly inspiring.

00:04:01.049 --> 00:04:03.479
And I'm sorry if I don't write everyone back.

00:04:03.479 --> 00:04:05.180
Trust me I'm trying!

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:08.040
So thank you, thank you and thank you.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:12.400
This time of year is when we give thanks and
show gratitude and it's all of you who have

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:16.260
given me so much to be thankful and grateful
for.

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:21.760
I look forward to kicking off 2018 with you
soon enough but in the mean time Merry Christmas,

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:24.760
Happy Hannukah, happy new year and May The
Force Be With You.

